== Purpose ==
The LastRevision template displays the last revision date of a specified MediaWiki page in a human-readable format (Month DD, YYYY).

== Syntax ==
 <code><nowiki>{{LastRevision|page_name}}</nowiki></code>

== Parameters ==
{| class="fandom-table"
!Parameter
!Description
!Required
!Default
|-
|<code>1</code> (unnamed)
|The name of the page to check
|No
|Current page name
|}

== Examples ==

=== Basic Usage ===
 <code><nowiki>{{LastRevision|Mafumafu}}</nowiki></code>
Output: {{LastRevision|Mafumafu}}

=== Current Page ===
 <code><nowiki>{{LastRevision}}</nowiki></code>
Output: {{LastRevision}}

=== With Namespace ===
 <code><nowiki>{{LastRevision|Utaite Wiki:Tutorial}}</nowiki></code>
Output: {{LastRevision|Utaite Wiki:Tutorial}}

== Output Format ==
The template returns dates in the format: '''Month DD, YYYY'''

Examples of output formatting:

* <code>January 1, 2025</code>
* <code>March 15, 2024</code>
* <code>December 31, 2023</code>

== Technical Details ==
The template uses the following MediaWiki parser functions:

* <code>REVISIONTIMESTAMP</code> - Retrieves the timestamp of the last revision
* <code>#time</code> - Formats the timestamp into readable date format
* Template parameters with default fallback to <code>PAGENAME</code>

== Limitations ==

* Only works for pages that exist in the wiki
* Returns empty or error if the specified page doesn't exist
* Requires the page to have at least one revision
* Date reflects the last edit timestamp, not publication date
* Expensive function

